\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Praise to the Holiest in the height,
\par And in the depth be praise:
\par In all His words most wonderful;
\par Most sure in all His ways.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O living wisdom of our God!
\par When all was sin and shame,
\par A second Adam to the fight
\par And to the rescue came.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O wisest love! that flesh and blood
\par Which did in Adam fail,
\par Should strive afresh against the foe,
\par Should strive and should prevail.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And that a higher gift than grace
\par Should flesh and blood refine,
\par God's presence, and His very self
\par And essence all-divine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O generous love! that He, who smote
\par In man for man the foe,
\par The double agony in man
\par For man should undergo.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. And in the garden secretly,
\par And on the Cross on high,
\par Should teach His brethren, and inspire
\par To suffer and to die.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Praise to the Holiest in the height,
\par And in the depth be praise:
\par In all His words most wonderful;
\par Most sure in all His ways.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

